    <string name="help_body">"Turn on the device, then choose it in the app or connect to its Wi-Fi manually. Stabilization uses the starting orientation as its reference. Mirror flips the image.\n\nChoose an ear side before taking a photo, or label an existing photo in its details. Compare two photos of the same ear in the gallery. Media is saved to the active care profile, and recordings capture device video only.\n\nWhen reporting a problem, include your phone model, OS version, steps and diagnostic log. GitHub is public. Keep personal and clinical images private."</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">"The app receives device images over local Wi-Fi. It uses no accounts, advertising, analytics or cloud sync.\n\nProfile names, photos, ear labels, silent videos, known device Wi-Fi details and diagnostic logs are stored on your phone. Android requires permission to read the Wi-Fi list when finding nearby devices. The app does not access GPS, the system photo library, the microphone or Bluetooth.\n\nWhen you tap Share, Android passes your selected files to the app you choose. You can delete files from the gallery. Clearing app data or uninstalling removes its local data. Recipients control copies you have already shared.\n\nFor privacy questions or feedback, contact GitHub @foreverfine77."</string>
